# Normalise all text to LF in the repository and on checkout. Without this, a Windows
# checkout stores CRLF and a macOS/Linux collaborator sees whole-file diffs that bury the
# real change — and prettier and git end up fighting each other on every commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts break outright with CRLF line endings (the shebang picks up the \r), so be
# explicit even though the rule above already covers them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
